title: You are summoned by the King
new-page: true

## News arrived that the King officially summons you
## Finished, but needs further polishing

- @meet_1: A summoning decree has arrived.

@meet_1
subtitle: From none other than the King of Nocturnia himself.
new-page: true

It obviously does not take long for the news to spread far and wide. With the newspaper's extensive publication network, the ground-breaking headline is sure to take the attention of many people, inside and even outside the kingdom.

And so it doesn't surprise you when one of the King's butlers soon approaches you and Princess Darlyne together to inform that the King of Nocturnia wants to summon both of you this afternoon.

"Salutations, Your Highness, Sir Levon," the butler greets as he gives a deep bow. "I am here to inform that the King demands both of you to be in his presence as soon as possible." 

- @what_for: "What for, if we may know?"
- @alright: "Alright, we understand."

@what_for

"What for, if we may know?" you ask first. You could quite easily deduce the reason behind the King's summoning, but it's often better to just confirm it straight away.

"For..." the butler hesitates for a bit, and his gaze briefly shifts away from you. "...For issues that have arisen in relation to the Princess' activity recently."

You lift your eyebrows slightly. That is a much vaguer answer than you had expected.

"I apologize if that is not clear," the butler immediately replies with a curt nod, as if he could see what you were thinking about before. "But that is all that we could disclose for now."

You briefly share a glance with Princess Darlyne. She looks composed enough from the outside, but for you who have seen her so many times, you could notice her slightly trembling hand and quietly shaken expression.

- @alright: "Alright, we understand."

@alright

"Alright, we understand." You share another glance with Princess Darlyne. "Let us go, Your Highness."

Princess Darlyne gives an assured nod. Though you could see that she was anxious before, her eyes are now looking more determined than ever.

As you bid a respectful nod to the butler, Princess Darlyne walks ahead, with you not far behind.

- @time_to_go: It's time to go.

@time_to_go
new-page: true

- @king_meet: The King of Nocturnia is inside.

@king_meet
subtitle: You wonder what awaits behind the majestic door.
new-page: true

The two of you step inside as the guard opens the vast door. The King, you notice, sits still on top of the throne at the end of the room.

The red carpet, which you had walked not too rarely, suddenly feels wider than ever before. Your heart beats with increasing intensity as you kneel together with Princess Darlyne in front of the King.

It almost feels like a lifetime when the King finally speaks.

"Greetings, Levon, and... my daughter," the King trails off slightly at the end.

- @greet: "With our utmost respect, we greet, Your Majesty." 

@greet

"With our utmost respect, we greet, Your Majesty." 

As you finish your greetings, the King gestures both of you to stand up.

"I think..." the King takes a deep breath as he pauses. "...the two of you have understood the reason behind why I am summoning the two of you here."

You gulp inwardly as you nod. "Yes, Your Grace."

The King lets out a long sigh.

"Before I begin... I would like for everyone in here  — with the exception of Princess Darlyne and her assistant — to exit this room at once."

Silently, the guards standing next to the throne disperse, and you can also hear footsteps getting further away from where you are standing.

As the sound of footsteps slowly disappear, you can hear the doors closing from way behind you...

